TITLE:: RCKeyProxy
summary:: One key of a beat's pattern: its source, its seed, its live edits
categories:: Libraries>reCurrent
related:: Classes/RCPbindProxy, Classes/RCBeat, Classes/PatternProxy, Classes/Pseed

DESCRIPTION::
Replaces the code::PatternProxy:: + code::Pseed:: + code::Pcollect:: stack that code::PbindProxy:: gave every key of an link::Classes/RCBeat::. That stack ran two to four Routines per key per event (a static value alone costs two) and a closure per value. The stream of a proxy, code::RCKeyStream::, reads a static value with code::.next:: (a code::Ref:: dereferences, an code::Event:: composes, as under code::PatternProxy::) and runs every other source in one Routine of its own.

Seeded output is bit-identical to the old stack: a seeded Pattern or Function runs in a Routine with code::randSeed = seed:: (Pseed's own construction); an unseeded one shares the creating thread's random state, as any new Routine does (a Routine that never seeded itself shares its parents' state up to the thread that last did); a Stream given as a value is used as is, never re-seeded.

Live edits (link::#-setSource::) land where code::PatternProxy:: landed them: with a nil quant the new source gives the next value; with a number, code::[beats, phase]:: or code::Quant:: the grid time is taken at the first pull after the edit, the old source plays until then, gets one more (discarded) pull at the switch and the new one takes over; a later edit whose grid comes first wins and drops the earlier one; an old source that ends before its grid hands over at once.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: key
argument:: source
A static value, a Function or code::Pfunc::, a Pattern or a Stream.
argument:: seed
A random seed for the source, or nil.
argument:: clock
The clock whose grid live edits use.
argument:: mirror
When true (the default), link::#-lastValue:: records every non-static value (link::Classes/RCUtil#*isStatic::).

METHOD:: classify
code::\stream::, code::\pattern:: (a Pattern or a Function) or code::\static::: how a stream treats a source.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: setSource
A live edit: every stream of this proxy switches to the new source.
argument:: newSource
argument:: newQuant
nil: at the stream's next value; a number, code::[beats, phase]:: or code::Quant::: on that grid of link::#-clock::.
argument:: newSeed
nil leaves the new source unseeded, as link::Classes/RCBeat#-set:: does.

METHOD:: lastValue
The last value produced (nil for a static source).
METHOD:: thread
The Routine of a Pattern or Function source; nil for a static.
METHOD:: randData
The random state of the key's Routine. Settable, to replay a key.
METHOD:: key
METHOD:: source
METHOD:: seed
METHOD:: clock
METHOD:: quant
The quant of the latest edit.
METHOD:: mirror
METHOD:: version
Incremented by every edit; streams detect it at their next pull.
